From 35fc4a654ca629be18d954c402486d9221f6cdf2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phil Elwell <phil@raspberrypi.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 16:53:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: xhci-pci: Limit VL805 DMA address to 40 bits

Commit [1] forced a 36-bit DMA address width limit on VL805 XHCI
controllers, on the basis that the device can't handle any more. There
are Pi 5 HAT+ cards with VL805s to support more USB ports or attach
other USB-based device. This change breaks such HATs because the inbound
window is placed at 1x_xxxxxxxx - 37-bit addresses.

The fact that these HATs used to work suggests that at least some VL805s
don't have this restriction. Raise that limit to 40 bits - a width which
has been observed to be usable.

See: https://github.com/raspberrypi/linux/pull/7608
Signed-off-by: Phil Elwell <phil@raspberrypi.com>

[1] commit 1fc50f1ecde3 ("usb: xhci-pci: Limit VIA VL805 DMA addressing
    to 36 bits")
---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-pci.c
@@ -460,7 +460,7 @@ static void xhci_pci_quirks(struct devic
 	if (pdev->vendor == PCI_VENDOR_ID_VIA && pdev->device == PCI_DEVICE_ID_VIA_VL805) {
 		xhci->quirks |= XHCI_LPM_SUPPORT;
 		xhci->quirks |= XHCI_TRB_OVERFETCH;
-		xhci->dma_mask_bits = 37;
+		xhci->dma_mask_bits = 40;
 		xhci->quirks |= XHCI_EP_CTX_BROKEN_DCS;
 		xhci->quirks |= XHCI_AVOID_DQ_ON_LINK;
 		xhci->quirks |= XHCI_VLI_SS_BULK_OUT_BUG;
